<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 10.153 percent from 10.178 percent at the previous auction on November 21.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Feb 27, 1997 (Feb 20, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.153 percent (10.178)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 989.575 million (656.250 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1.86 billion (700.950 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.998-10.188 percent (10.002-10.204)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.998-10.242 percent (10.101-10.301)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 132 (101)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 166 (115)</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 Egyptian pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
